# CODEOWNERS for ophelian
#
# This file designates required reviewers for security-sensitive paths.
# GitHub uses it to auto-request reviews on pull requests, and — if
# branch protection on `main` has "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled — to *block* merges of those PRs until a code owner approves.
#
# Why this matters for `.github/`:
#   - `.github/workflows/*.yml` defines what runs in CI with repo
#     secrets and OIDC trust (PyPI Trusted Publishing, GitHub Pages,
#     etc.). A malicious or careless change here can exfiltrate
#     credentials or publish a poisoned release.
#   - `.github/dependabot.yml` controls which automated PRs Dependabot
#     opens; weakening it (e.g. disabling the github-actions ecosystem)
#     would silently let SHA-pinned actions rot.
#   - We pin every action to an immutable 40-char commit SHA, but a pin
#     is only as good as the human review of the bump PR. CODEOWNERS
#     guarantees that human is the release maintainer.
#
# Syntax: <pattern> <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Order matters — the *last* matching pattern wins for a given file.
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything, so nothing is unowned.
*                       @LuisFalva

# Anything under .github/ — workflows, dependabot config, issue
# templates, PR template — requires release-maintainer review.
/.github/               @LuisFalva
/.github/workflows/     @LuisFalva
/.github/dependabot.yml @LuisFalva

# CODEOWNERS itself: changes to the review policy must be reviewed by
# the same people the policy currently protects.
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @LuisFalva
